ABC HOSPITAL - HEALTHY FOODS SHOPPING CHECKLIST

Published by: ABC Hospital Oncology Department
Date: 2026
Pages: 5

CANCER-FRIENDLY GROCERY SHOPPING LIST

Patient Name: _____________________
Date: _____________________

GENERAL TIPS
✓ Shop when you're not tired or hungry
✓ Bring your list and stick to it
✓ Read labels for protein and calorie content
✓ Ask for help if you need it
✓ Consider online delivery if going out is difficult

PRODUCE SECTION

Fruits (choose variety):
□ Bananas (great for smoothies)
□ Berries (fresh or frozen)
□ Avocados (healthy fats)
□ Apples
□ Oranges and citrus
□ Melons
□ Mangoes
□ Peaches
□ Frozen fruit blends for smoothies

Vegetables:
□ Spinach and leafy greens
□ Carrots
□ Sweet potatoes
□ Broccoli
□ Cauliflower
□ Butternut squash
□ Peas (fresh or frozen)
□ Green beans
□ Bell peppers
□ Onions
□ Garlic
□ Ginger
□ Mushrooms

PROTEIN SECTION

Meat and Poultry:
□ Chicken (breasts, thighs)
□ Ground turkey
□ Lean beef
□ Eggs (excellent protein source)

Fish:
□ Salmon (omega-3 rich)
□ Tuna (canned in water)
□ White fish
□ Sardines

Plant-based:
□ Tofu
□ Tempeh
□ Edamame
□ Beans (canned or dried)
□ Lentils
□ Chickpeas

DAIRY AND ALTERNATIVES

□ Milk (regular or plant-based)
□ Yogurt (Greek for extra protein)
□ Cheese (variety)
□ Cottage cheese
□ Kefir
□ Almond milk
□ Soy milk
□ Oat milk

GRAINS

□ Oats (rolled or quick)
□ Quinoa
□ Brown rice
□ White rice (if needed for soft diet)
□ Pasta (regular or protein-enriched)
□ Whole grain bread
□ Crackers (plain)
□ Rice cakes
□ Cereal (low sugar)

HEALTHY FATS

□ Olive oil
□ Coconut oil
□ Nut butters (peanut, almond)
□ Nuts (almonds, walnuts, cashews)
□ Seeds (chia, flax, pumpkin)
□ Hummus

CANNED AND JARRED FOODS

□ Soups (low sodium)
□ Broth (chicken, vegetable)
□ Canned fruits (in juice, not syrup)
□ Canned vegetables
□ Tomato sauce
□ Coconut milk
□ Nut butters
□ Jam or honey

SNACKS AND EXTRAS

□ Protein bars
□ Granola
□ Trail mix
□ Dried fruit
□ Pudding cups
□ Applesauce
□ Gelatin
□ Crackers
□ Rice cakes

BEVERAGES

□ Water
□ Herbal teas (ginger, peppermint)
□ 100% fruit juices
□ Vegetable juices
□ Sports drinks (if needed)
□ Protein shakes

SUPPLEMENTS (if recommended)

□ Protein powder
□ Meal replacement shakes
□ Multivitamin
□ Specific supplements as prescribed

SPECIALTY ITEMS

□ Thickening products (if needed)
□ Pureed foods
□ Tube feeding supplies (if applicable)

